@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: cli-sum-stdin
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, cli, stdin]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "timeparse CLI gains --sum, '-' stdin input, and all-errors-at-once validation"
+---
+
+# SPEC: cli-sum-stdin
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`timeparse.cli.main` stops at the first invalid duration and can only take durations from argv. The ask adds a total mode, stdin input, and a complete error report so a caller sees every bad input in one run.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+- `--sum` prints only the total seconds, on one line.
+- `-` as a duration argument reads durations from stdin, mixed in order with other arguments.
+- Every invalid input is reported on stderr in one run; stdout stays empty and the exit code is 2.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: sum of arguments
+**Given** argv `["--sum", "1h", "30m"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `5400\n` and it returns 0
+
+### S2: stdin mixed with sum
+**Given** stdin `"1m\n\n2m\n"` and argv `["-", "--sum"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `180\n` and it returns 0
+
+### S3: all invalid inputs reported
+**Given** argv `["1h", "x", "2q"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stderr is exactly `error: invalid duration: 'x'\nerror: invalid duration: '2q'\n`, stdout is empty, and it returns 2
+
+### S4: default output and input order
+**Given** stdin `"  30s \n"` and argv `["1h", "-", "1m"]` without `--sum`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is `3600\n30\n60\n` and it returns 0
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- New duration syntax or changes to `parse_duration`.
+- Output formats other than plain integer seconds.
+- Streaming stdin or reading files.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | existing `tests/test_cli.py` uses it with `capsys` |
+| Compatibility | `main(argv) -> int` signature unchanged | existing callers and tests |
+| Scope | `timeparse/cli.py` only (plus tests) | the ask names that file |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_s1_sum_args` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_s2_stdin_sum` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_s3_all_invalid_reported` |
+| S4 | unit | `test_s4_order_and_default_output` |
+
+### AC-001: Sum prints only the total
+Covers S1. Oracle: golden, `1h + 30m = 3600 + 1800 = 5400`.
+
+### AC-002: Dash reads stdin, blanks ignored
+Covers S2, S4. Oracle: golden, the example in the ask (`1m + 2m = 180`).
+
+### AC-003: Every invalid input reported, nothing on stdout
+Covers S3. Oracle: golden, the example in the ask.
+
+### AC-004: Default output is one line per duration in input order
+Covers S4. Oracle: golden, hand-computed from the unit table.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one file, one session, no irreversible decision. The CLI change is additive and fully specified by the ask, so the stage ran no interview round (autopilot `auto_full`, no question asked).
+- Defaults chosen where the ask is silent: argv items are stripped like stdin lines before parsing and reporting; an empty argv string is invalid (text `''`); a repeated `-` reads stdin once and the later `-` contributes nothing; `-` with empty stdin yields no durations, so `--sum` prints `0` and plain mode prints nothing; `--sum` with invalid input prints nothing on stdout.
+- Spec-validator not dispatched: light lane with `irreversible_decisions: []`.
